  "problem": "Simon measures the temperature of the tea in his cup, and the thermometer displays a reading of ${60}^{\u2218}C.$ After $10$ minutes, Simon repeats the measurement and the thermometer displays a reading of  ${52}^{\u2218}C.$ To the nearest minute, how long does it take for the tea to decrease its temperature to ${40}^{\u2218}C$ if the temperature in the room is ${28}^{\u2218}C?$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that the temperature $T(t)$ of the tea in Simon's cup decreases at a rate that obeys Newton's law of cooling, where $T$ is measured in degrees Celsius and $t>0$ is the time, in minutes, since the first measurement.*",
